T76	Quotation 15947 16333	"a most natural feeling; and the longer it lasts, the better I shall be pleased.  But here is my father coming: you will not object to my reading the charade to him.  It will be giving him so much pleasure! He loves any thing of the sort, and especially any thing that pays woman a compliment.  He has the tenderest spirit of gallantry towards us all!-- You must let me read it to him."
R101	Cueing Arg1:T74 Arg2:T73	
R102	Cueing Arg1:T74 Arg2:T76	
