T221	Quotation 46532 46575	"And do you see her, sir, tolerably often?"
T222	Cue 46576 46581	asked
T223	Entity 46582 46590	Isabella
R294	Cueing Arg1:T222 Arg2:T221	
R295	Speaker Arg1:T223 Arg2:T221	
T224	Entity 46643 46656	Mr. Woodhouse
T225	Cue 46657 46666	hesitated
T226	Quotation 46670 46716	"Not near so often, my dear, as I could wish."
T227	Quotation 46717 47428	"Oh! papa, we have missed seeing them but one entire day since they married.  Either in the morning or evening of every day, excepting one, have we seen either Mr. Weston or Mrs. Weston, and generally both, either at Randalls or here-- and as you may suppose, Isabella, most frequently here.  They are very, very kind in their visits.  Mr. Weston is really as kind as herself.  Papa, if you speak in that melancholy way, you will be giving Isabella a false idea of us all.  Every body must be aware that Miss Taylor must be missed, but every body ought also to be assured that Mr. and Mrs. Weston do really prevent our missing her by any means to the extent we ourselves anticipated-- which is the exact truth."
R296	Cueing Arg1:T225 Arg2:T226	
R297	Speaker Arg1:T224 Arg2:T226	
R298	Addressee Arg1:T223 Arg2:T226	
R299	Speaker Arg1:T223 Arg2:T227	
R300	Addressee Arg1:T224 Arg2:T227	
T228	Quotation 47429 47452	"Just as it should be,"
T229	Cue 47453 47457	said
T230	Entity 47458 47477	Mr. John Knightley,
T231	Quotation 47478 47837	"and just as I hoped it was from your letters.  Her wish of shewing you attention could not be doubted, and his being a disengaged and social man makes it all easy.  I have been always telling you, my love, that I had no idea of the change being so very material to Hartfield as you apprehended; and now you have Emma's account, I hope you will be satisfied."
R301	Cueing Arg1:T229 Arg2:T228	
R302	Cueing Arg1:T229 Arg2:T231	
