R347	Addressee Arg1:T254 Arg2:T257	
T258	Quotation 50240 50731	"Three-and-twenty!-- is he indeed?-- Well, I could not have thought it-- and he was but two years old when he lost his poor mother!  Well, time does fly indeed!-- and my memory is very bad.  However, it was an exceeding good, pretty letter, and gave Mr. and Mrs. Weston a great deal of pleasure.  I remember it was written from Weymouth, and dated Sept. 28th-- and began, 'My dear Madam,' but I forget how it went on; and it was signed 'F. C. Weston Churchill.'-- I remember that perfectly."
