T262	Quotation 50816 51211	"I have no doubt of his being a most amiable young man. But how sad it is that he should not live at home with his father! There is something so shocking in a child's being taken away from his parents and natural home!  I never could comprehend how Mr. Weston could part with him.  To give up one's child!  I really never could think well of any body who proposed such a thing to any body else."
