T308	Quotation 58303 58514	"Mr. Wingfield most strenuously recommended it, sir-- or we should not have gone.  He recommended it for all the children, but particularly for the weakness in little Bella's throat,-- both sea air and bathing."
T309	Quotation 58515 58773	"Ah! my dear, but Perry had many doubts about the sea doing her any good; and as to myself, I have been long perfectly convinced, though perhaps I never told you so before, that the sea is very rarely of use to any body.  I am sure it almost killed me once."
