T314	Quotation 59089 59127	"Oh! good Mr. Perry-- how is he, sir?"
T315	Quotation 59128 59465	"Why, pretty well; but not quite well.  Poor Perry is bilious, and he has not time to take care of himself-- he tells me he has not time to take care of himself-- which is very sad-- but he is always wanted all round the country.  I suppose there is not a man in such practice anywhere.  But then there is not so clever a man any where."
T316	Quotation 59466 59651	"And Mrs. Perry and the children, how are they? do the children grow? I have a great regard for Mr. Perry.  I hope he will be calling soon. He will be so pleased to see my little ones."
