T381	Quotation 74049 74748	"It is so cold, so very cold-- and looks and feels so very much like snow, that if it were to any other place or with any other party, I should really try not to go out to-day-- and dissuade my father from venturing; but as he has made up his mind, and does not seem to feel the cold himself, I do not like to interfere, as I know it would be so great a disappointment to Mr. and Mrs. Weston.  But, upon my word, Mr. Elton, in your case, I should certainly excuse myself.  You appear to me a little hoarse already, and when you consider what demand of voice and what fatigues to-morrow will bring, I think it would be no more than common prudence to stay at home and take care of yourself to-night."
